%% Negative SRSW fixture.  glp.tex Remark "Guards and SRSW": a guard whose
%% success implies its argument is ground lets both X and X? occur multiple
%% times, and "guards such as known and compound do not imply groundness:
%% known(X?) succeeds when X? is bound to f(Y?) with Y? unbound."
%%
%% So known/1 licenses no multiple occurrence, and X? occurring twice in the
%% body under it is an SRSW violation.  The positive counterpart, where the
%% guard IS groundness-implying, is srsw/ground_guard_multi_ok.glp.
procedure k(_?, _).
k(X, Y?) :- known(X?) | pair(X?, X?, Y).

procedure pair(_?, _?, _).
pair(_, _, done).
